   "sense: 'kende klokken' means 'to know what time it is' (by looking at a clock), not 'to know the time (on a clock)' as a general ability. The Danish sentence 'Kan du kende klokken på den store urskive?' is unnatural and does not clearly show the meaning; a native speaker would say 'Kan du se, hvad klokken er, på den store urskive?' or similar.",
   "translations: The English translation 'Can you tell the time on the big dial?' is unnatural; 'tell the time' is a general skill, not used for a specific clock face. The Russian 'Ты можешь определить время по большому циферблату?' and Ukrainian 'Ти можеш визначити час за великим циферблатом?' are also unnatural for the same reason.",
   "adjudicator: The Danish sentence 'Kan du kende klokken på den store urskive?' is unnatural; a native speaker would say 'Kan du se, hvad klokken er, på den store urskive?' and the translations incorrectly treat 'tell the time' as a specific instance rather than a general skill."
  ]
